&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have you ever wished an app worked a little better?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Testlio, we help some of the world&#39;s leading technology and consumer brands improve their apps and digital products by collecting feedback from real people. Our global community of freelance testers has helped companies deliver better experiences to millions of users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re currently looking for people based in &lt;strong&gt;Brazil or Mexico who are current paid subscribers of Instagram+&lt;/strong&gt; (Instagram&#39;s paid subscription) to take part in a user research study about their experience with the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No professional software testing experience is required. If you&#39;re comfortable sharing honest feedback and recording yourself on video, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must currently live in Brazil or Mexico&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must have an active, paid Instagram+ subscription (not a free trial) that you&#39;ve held for more than 1 month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must use Instagram on an iPhone or Android smartphone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must be willing to share your Instagram username so your subscription status can be verified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You should be comfortable completing the study in English or your native language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must be comfortable recording and uploading short, selfie-style video responses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does testing look like?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Type of testing: User research (paid subscription experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Type of work: Short-term, freelance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure: Two sessions approximately 7 days apart, with light ongoing attention to your Instagram use in between.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time commitment: Approximately 1.5–2 hours total across both sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pay rate: 12 USD/hr.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payment: You are paid weekly via PayPal or Payoneer, in USD, which you can convert to your local currency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits of being a freelancer at Testlio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule: You can create your own schedule and take on other testing runs that interest you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Testlio is a 100% remote company. Work from wherever suits you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth: You&#39;ll be contributing to research for a global-scale app and building experience along the way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payment: You&#39;re paid by the hour, not by the bug, so you get paid regardless of what you find.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to start?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please fill out the initial application. Those who meet the requirements will receive further information to participate in this paid research opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Testlio&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testlio’s fully managed crowdsourced testing platform, powered by our proprietary intelligence technology – LeoAI Engine&lt;sup&gt;TM&lt;/sup&gt;, integrates expert, on-demand testers directly into your release process. Ship faster and more confidently with global coverage across 600,000+ devices, 800+ payment methods, 150+ countries, and 100+ languages. To learn more, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.testlio.com&quot;&gt;www.testlio.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job post is to keep in touch for future contract roles with Testlio. If you would like to freelance test with us you can learn more and sign up &lt;a href=&quot;https://testlio.com/work/freelancer/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About this job post:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job post is for &lt;strong&gt;future opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;. If there isn’t an active opening that fits your skill set or location, you can still express interest in future roles with Testlio. Our Talent Acquisition team will keep your information on file and reach out if a suitable opportunity becomes available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Typical Project Details:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Focus&lt;/strong&gt;: You will be a Software Quality Assurance Analyst following Agile methodologies, mostly focused on API testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Duration&lt;/strong&gt;: Contracts can be temporary, ranging from 6 months to 1 year, or ongoing. Many temporary projects extend beyond their initial term, and some evolve into ongoing contractor opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: This job ad is open to candidates in select countries who are comfortable working in a fully remote setup. Countries we are considering consist of Argentina,&amp;nbsp;Brazil, Canada, the&amp;nbsp;Czech Republic,&amp;nbsp;Estonia,&amp;nbsp;India,&amp;nbsp;Ireland,&amp;nbsp;Mexico,&amp;nbsp;Poland,&amp;nbsp;Portugal, Romania, Spain,&amp;nbsp;Ukraine, the&amp;nbsp;United Kingdom, or the&amp;nbsp;United States.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schedule&lt;/strong&gt;: Opportunities are available for both part-time and full-time contracts. Working hours generally follow day or afternoon schedules based on your regional time zone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Timezone&lt;/strong&gt;: While we support flexible work, most roles align with standard daytime hours in their region (e.g., 9 AM–6 PM). For instance, this may mean Central Standard Time (CST) in the Americas or Central European Time (CET) in EMEA. Please ensure your availability aligns with your region’s core hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Devices&lt;/strong&gt;: You must have access to an Android or iOS mobile device for testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internet Connection&lt;/strong&gt;: A reliable, high-speed internet connection is required for testing and team communications. Mobile hotspots and other unstable or limited connections are not suitable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Your Day Looks Like&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute smoke, scripted, and exploratory test cases on mobile, web and desktop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct functional, localization, regression, and payments testing to ensure software meets quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report, reproduce, and track issues found during testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and share test results, including bugs and potential risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze test results, logs, and related data to identify patterns, trends, and areas for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with developers, product managers, and other stakeholders to align on goals, timelines, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate test progress, issues, and risks clearly and proactively with stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate test reports that provide actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute API tests using tools like Postman, SoapUI, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, maintain, and review test cases and test suites aligned with business priorities and industry best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and optimize effective test data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the test library remains relevant by refactoring, updating, and deprecating tests as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain a deep understanding of the systems under test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date with trends and advancements in software testing tools and methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Need to Succeed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience (2+ years) as a QA Analyst or similar role, with a strong understanding of software testing principles, methodologies, and tools (such as JIRA, Bugzilla, TestRail, Xray or similar.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile and web applications, frontend and backend testing (including API testing.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in identifying and documenting software bugs and issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to solve technical tasks required during testing - such as test data generation, log capturing and basic analysis, working with browser developer tools, network logs analyzers, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working in agile teams in a remote environment - proven track record of communication and collaboration with different stakeholders such as Scrum Masters, Product Owners and others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good knowledge of SDLC, CI/CD, and DevOps, as well as an understanding of test automation principles in effective SDLC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Human Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective English communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate and work effectively in a team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive to learn quickly and continuously expand knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with a frequently changing environment and able to adapt fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and the ability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What is the Consideration Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whenever a new opportunity arises, the Talent Acquisition team will review applicants and reach out to begin learning more. If you are a potential match, the recruiter will reach out to give you more details about the role and begin your application process&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testlio is an equal-opportunity employer deeply committed to creating an inclusive environment for people of all backgrounds and identities. We are female-founded, and 46% of our team members identify as women. See the &lt;a href=&quot;https://testlio.com/diversity-equity-and-inclusion/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;DEI section&lt;/a&gt; of our website for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
